  "worked_solution": "The truth set of $P\u2228Q$ represents the *union* of the truth sets of $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y):$\n\n$$\n{T}_{P\u2228Q}={T}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q}\n$$\n\nTherefore, to get the truth set of $P(x,y)\u2228Q(x,y),$ we take all the points that belong to ${T}_{P}$ or ${T}_{Q},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14099242/assets/097203c1cb185dbd1831bb4b4c50b0706286633ba2cee57847490e0ef467d180.png)\n\n**Note:** The points where the *solid* line meets the *dashed* curve belong to ${T}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q}$ since these points lie in ${T}_{P}.$",
